EXT. FLOODED RICE PADDY - PUMP HOUSE ROOF - DUSK

Sky bruised orange. Frogs. Somewhere, far off, the thump of mortars. Not close. Not yet.

SGT. KOSTAS VLAHOS, 40s, lies prone behind a sandbag. Rifle across his forearms. He hasn't blinked in a minute.

PVT. ELIAS TREMBLAY, 19, crouches beside him. Boots soaked. He chews a strip of dry rice cake.

CPL. HANA YOSHIDA, 30s, the radio operator, sits cross-legged under a tarp. Headset on one ear.

TREMBLAY
How long do we sit here?

VLAHOS
Till he says.

Tremblay glances at the radio. She shakes her head. He sinks back.

YOSHIDA
Static. Nothing but static.

Frogs go quiet. All three freeze. He lifts a hand. She stops breathing. The boy stops chewing.

A beat. The frogs start again.

TREMBLAY
(whispering)
Was that us?

VLAHOS
Wind.

He doesn't believe it. Neither do they. She slides the headset off, lays it on her knee.

YOSHIDA
They moved the line.

VLAHOS
How far?

YOSHIDA
Behind us.

Silence. The mortars are louder now. Tremblay reaches for his rifle, fumbles it. It clatters on tin.

They duck. All three. Eyes up.

Across the paddy, a flashlight blinks once. Twice.

VLAHOS
Get down.

TREMBLAY
Sarge--

VLAHOS
DOWN.

The water around the pump house shivers. Then the roof lifts.

A white flash swallows everything.
